<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I8d30673e73d3e785c3ae560063d2c6ec4d1e1b3e" commit="cb68d4056584196286c5f73620c8eb8dcc1e8f53" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/img-rogue: Include TLA in busy time statistic  Include GPU active low statistic (, i.e., the time the Texture Load Accelerator is active) in busy time reported to DEVFREQ.  Flash animation which exercised TLA showed poor performance due to frequency not being increased. This is due to TLA time not being included in busy time reported to DEVFREQ.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51393 TEST=WebGL Aquarium, Flash animation and look at GPU freq.  Change-Id: I8d30673e73d3e785c3ae560063d2c6ec4d1e1b3e Signed-off-by: Rufus Hamade &lt;rufus.hamade@imgtec.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/348690 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="348690" owner_email="rufus.hamade@imgtec.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/90/348690/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="If927bfbe1686fe9a2d7a5899041f10b53e149259" commit="7c88f41619e7fa40a9349688452d772840a98f19" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/img-rogue: Dump decoded firmware trace  Add the infrastructure to allow the kernel module to dump a decoded version of the firmware trace.  To see this trace, read /sys/kernel/debug/pvr/firmware_trace.  Although, to see anything interesting, you first have to enable firmware trace, e.g., via running the command: pvrdebug -loggroups main,mts  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53989 TEST=Boot to UI.  Read firmware_trace.  Change-Id: If927bfbe1686fe9a2d7a5899041f10b53e149259 Signed-off-by: Rufus Hamade &lt;rufus.hamade@imgtec.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/349041 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="349041" owner_email="rufus.hamade@imgtec.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/41/349041/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I3d8c6dd3422df75e0a8411f3c2945bde8196fa34" commit="452db51fdaee127d2a521f89fe0169096c02cf54" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/img-rogue: Eliminate use of global in debug_dump  The dubug_dump debugfs file was not thread safe.  Reading the file from multiple threads could cause a kernel crash.  This change removes global variables and passes file pointers as stack variables.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53989 TEST=Boot to UI, read /sys/kernel/debug/pvr/debug_dump  Change-Id: I3d8c6dd3422df75e0a8411f3c2945bde8196fa34 Signed-off-by: Rufus Hamade &lt;rufus.hamade@imgtec.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/349042 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="349042" owner_email="rufus.hamade@imgtec.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/42/349042/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I38a77dc62674e9a670b5a78152acd20eb825d5df" commit="d3402ac0b4c5e5eb0725ef1496c35df355414819" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/img-rogue: Remove DRM_POWERVR_ROGUE_KERNEL_SRVINIT  UM firmware load is no longer supported, so remove the build option that enables it.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53989 TEST=Boot to UI  Change-Id: I38a77dc62674e9a670b5a78152acd20eb825d5df Signed-off-by: Rufus Hamade &lt;rufus.hamade@imgtec.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/349043 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="349043" owner_email="rufus.hamade@imgtec.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/43/349043/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ic5c7021293cbd29e183a307a3b792f9036852513" commit="17d51549b03420119722f6d2b083ed46fce3b1e6" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/img-rogue: Rename bridge files  Upstream DDK has renamed the autogenerated &quot;direct&quot; bridge files. Do the rename here to make applying future patches easier.  Also, make the autogenerated bridge headers self-contained by getting them to include the headers they need rather than just relying on the .c file to do so.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53989 TEST=Boot to UI.  Change-Id: Ic5c7021293cbd29e183a307a3b792f9036852513 Signed-off-by: Rufus Hamade &lt;rufus.hamade@imgtec.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/349044 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="349044" owner_email="rufus.hamade@imgtec.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/44/349044/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3bfcc8eaa54c4559fe7d4c28dd74f030ebc8455c" commit="2ec28fc47271db99c61cdf9a92dd43e61362288e" commit_message="vboot: ec: Store vboot hash for EC image in a separate file  CBFS attributes are mostly useful for uses within CBFS itself, such as the transparent compression. Using the CBFS hash attribute for vboot causes multiple problems: it forces us to use hashes that CBFS can understand and generate on its own (whereas for some of our newer PD chips we'd like to feed vboot a &quot;hash&quot; that's not really a hash at all, but just a version number), and it prevents us from compressing the EC images in CBFS (since the CBFS hash attribute was originally designed for verification and thus always hashes the compressed data). Things will become easier if we just split these two distinct things apart.  This patch instead just assumes that for every EC image file X, there is also a file X.hash which contains the vboot hash for it (e.g. &quot;ecrw.hash&quot;). When vboot asks us for the hash we look up this hash file, and when it asks us for the full image we look up the normal image file. The hashes will be precomputed by the build system in a way that allows customization per chip type.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:348054 BRANCH=None BUG=chrome-os-partner:53780 TEST=Forced software sync on Oak in multiple scenarios.  Change-Id: I3bfcc8eaa54c4559fe7d4c28dd74f030ebc8455c Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/348061 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="348061" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/61/348061/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If08193b273b08e2fd52918a6a3608f7c100171a1" commit="9d6e72648cb1c2f386ba4b02d0898c3d547fc4ea" commit_message="coreboot, chromeos-ec: Put vboot hash in an extra file  This patch adapts our ebuilds to the new change in depthcharge that looks up vboot's hash for an EC image in a separate CBFS file. It is now the responsibility of every EC ebuild to generate an ec.RW.hash file next to ec.RW.bin, which will be added to CBFS by the coreboot ebuild. For the Chrome EC this file just contains a normal SHA256 hash, but other EC types can use &quot;hash&quot; formats more suitable to their capabilities.  With these changes, we can now also LZMA-compress the EC images in CBFS without disturbing software sync.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:348061 BUG=chrome-os-partner:53780 TEST=Built and booted Oak (including software sync).  Change-Id: If08193b273b08e2fd52918a6a3608f7c100171a1 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/348054 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="348054" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/54/348054/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I918dd121765f6a59d4886943484adcf2ea04c735" commit="e5dc532ac3a479cae672d060ba2d6104355ca0df" commit_message="EXPERIMENTAL: Add glimmer-cheets overlay (ARC++ on baytrail)  BUG=b:28634526 TEST=Can manually start android service and get on android shell      But it waits for arc bridge service. Change-Id: I918dd121765f6a59d4886943484adcf2ea04c735 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/348451 Commit-Ready: Rajat Jain &lt;rajatja@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Rajat Jain &lt;rajatja@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="348451" owner_email="rajatja@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/51/348451/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I10e4397c1c08ba999ca616a4f2102ffd97cbaecb" commit="e4de710a09f0968e5e797e4231ef42dd3fc11c02" commit_message="CHROMIUM: config: Change Intel audio drivers from y to m  While bringing up 3.18 on baytrail, I noticed errors such as: sst-acpi 80860F28:00: Direct firmware load for intel/fw_sst_0f28.bin-48kHz_i2s_master failed with error -2  The reason is that the sst-acpi driver is built into the kernel, and the /lib/firmware is not populated when the kernel boots up. This issue gets fixed and firmware gets loaded once we built the drivers that select CONFIG_SND_SOC_INTEL_SST_ACPI, as modules (since the /lib/modules is populated by the time modules are initializing).  Essentially I set: CONFIG_SND_SOC_INTEL_CHT_BSW_MAX98090_TI_MACH=m (currently =y) CONFIG_SND_SOC_INTEL_CHT_BSW_RT5645_MACH=m (currently =y) and they set the other configs to =m on running oldconfig.  BUG=b:28634526 TEST=Verified firmware load on baytrail systems Signed-off-by: Rajat Jain &lt;rajatja@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I10e4397c1c08ba999ca616a4f2102ffd97cbaecb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/348940 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="348940" owner_email="rajatja@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/40/348940/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia5b47b687f159ee5668ca4c17c28be16b659cd46" commit="c4faa0dc6b2e03a529a0ec194d6378a3ceafab01" commit_message="dut: implement file-based VPD.  Currently only Chromebook has the VPD partition and command. For other system, we may have a partition that is Read-only after shipping as VPD. Therefore, we need to implement a system VPD module that is file-based.  BUG=None TEST=Manually  Change-Id: Ia5b47b687f159ee5668ca4c17c28be16b659cd46 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/349441 Commit-Ready: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ting Shen &lt;phoenixshen@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="349441" owner_email="shunhsingou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/41/349441/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifa10eb500f172108006694ff6f51839c9faea658" commit="847b70f26c808246b5b2528341d79251860bb1b0" commit_message="elm: eq and volume tuning  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53981 TEST=`emerge-elm chromeos-bsp-elm`  Change-Id: Ifa10eb500f172108006694ff6f51839c9faea658 Signed-off-by: T.H. Lin &lt;T.H_Lin@quantatw.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/349490 Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="349490" owner_email="T.H_Lin@quantatw.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/90/349490/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8406.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>